    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 270 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` field on the owner response, formatted as `'LastName, FirstName'`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` string property (read-only, derived) to the `Owner` schema. Since `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec, this gives the DTO a `displayName` field on the response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBoth the create responder (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and the GET responder (`RespondWithOwner`) route through `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so the derived field appears consistently on both the POST create response and subsequent GETs \u2014 which is exactly how the `Cp06Tests` acceptance test reads it back.\n\nThe new `Cp06Tests` passes and all 270 existing tests remain green.",
